---
<LandingLayout
  title="ProRata.ai and Gist, and FORA — FORA resources"
  description="How ProRata pays publishers a share of each Gist answer, what Gist Answers needs from your site, where ProRata is ahead of FORA, and how a publisher can run both on the same site."
>
  <AudienceHero
    current="resources"
    badge={`Resources · ${a('/resources/content-marketplaces/', 'Content marketplaces')} · ProRata.ai and Gist`}
    title="ProRata pays you a share of each answer. <em>With FORA, you sell each access at your price.</em>"
    sub="ProRata.ai licenses your articles into its own answer engine, Gist, and pays you from a pool by how much of each answer your content supplied. FORA lets AI agents, software that fetches content for an AI system or its user, buy each access at the terms and price you set."
    updated={resourceUpdated(HREF)}
  >
    <a href="#ahead" class="btn btn-primary">Where ProRata is ahead</a>
    <a href="#together" class="btn btn-ghost">Run both</a>
  </AudienceHero>

  <Band tone="near" id="glance" label="At a glance" title="ProRata and FORA, side by side">
    <GlanceCard vendor="ProRata.ai and Gist" groups={GLANCE} />
  </Band>

  <Band label="The short answer" title="ProRata measures the answer. FORA prices the access.">
    <CardGrid items={SHORT_ANSWER} />
    <Callout kind="define" {...DEFINITIONS.exchange} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="light" id="paid" label="How you're paid" title="ProRata pays you monthly, from a pool, by your share of each answer" asideWidth="440px" asideAlign="start">
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <StepList items={PAID_STEPS} />
      <p class="prose" set:html={`Answers can also draw on sources outside the partner pool, such as Wikipedia (${a(P.guide, 'user guide')}). The contract doesn't say where their share goes (${a(P.msa, 'MSA §5')}).`} />
      <p class="prose" set:html={`ProRata retired its Gist Ads network "on September 1, 2026" (${a(P.ads, 'Gist Ads')}). It hasn't said what funds the pool since. It offers its attribution engine to AI platforms "through direct engagement with the team" (${a(P.products, 'Products')}) and names no platform customer.`} />
    </Fragment>
    <Figure
      slot="aside"
      src={`${IMG}/prorata-2.png`}
      title="Say a month brings ProRata $200,000 and 20 million valid answers: from its month to your payout."
      alt="Say a month brings ProRata $200,000 in net revenue and 20 million valid answers: each answer carries $0.01, and neither total is on your statement. Your month is $0.01 × 50% partner share × 25% average attribution × 30,000 answers = $37.50, which carries over, since ProRata pays by bank transfer only once you're owed more than $1,000."
    />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="near" compact label="ProRata in four numbers">
    <KeyFacts items={KEY_FACTS} />
  </Band>

  <Band label="How your articles get into answers" title="From your article to an answer, in four steps" asideWidth="440px" asideAlign="start">
    <StepList slot="intro" items={ARTICLE_STEPS} />
    <Figure
      slot="aside"
      src={`${IMG}/prorata-1.png`}
      title="From your article to your share of an answer."
      alt={'The WordPress plugin registers your posts feed, /wp-json/wp/v2/posts, and sends each post\'s address on save; ProRata\'s crawler reads the feed into ProRata\'s index of partner content, and the answer engine picks sources for the Gist widget on your pages and for ask.gist.ai. Each answer is split into claims, "atomic units of fact", matched to their sources to give an attribution percent per source: another partner, your article, or Wikipedia, which is not a partner.'}
    />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="light" label="Who has been paid so far" title="ProRata counts its partners and publishes no payout total">
    <p class="prose" set:html={`The Gist Answers page counts "150+" publishing partners and "1,600+" licensed titles (vendor's own data, ${a(P.answers, 'Gist Answers')}). No payout total is published.`} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="near" label="What Gist Answers needs from your site" title="The WordPress plugin or a script tag, an open feed, and an allow rule" lead="Readers and search crawlers reach your site as today. Gist needs no DNS change and no code on your CDN, but it touches your CMS, your cache rules and your bot protection. It runs through the WordPress plugin or one script tag; how Gist ingests a site that doesn't run WordPress isn't documented, so ask ProRata.">
    <Callout
      kind="engineers"
      collapse="Show the five points"
      text={`Every quote in this box is from Gist's ${a(P.guide, 'WordPress user guide')}, for plugin version 1.0.16.`}
      points={ENGINEERS}
    />
  </Band>

  <Band id="caution" label="What can go wrong" title="In Gist's own guide">
    <Callout kind="caution" points={CAUTIONS}>
      <PullQuote
        small
